 Any partial module is rolled back on failure. The first bounded error is
@@ -64,6 +68,11 @@ latched, no retry/fallback occurs, and all concurrent prewarm callers observe
 the same result. TensorIR, TileIR JIT, PTX, cuBLAS and framework fallback are
 not loader alternatives.
 
+CUDA Tile host launch dimensions are distinct from its physical worker-warp
+metadata. The reviewed launch ABI remains logical block `[1, 1, 1]`, as
+required by CUDA Tile; Cubin `EIATTR_REQNTID` records compiler-selected
+internal workers and must not be copied into `CUlaunchConfig.blockDim*`.
+
 Artifact v1 currently emits only static workspace size `0`, alignment `1`.
 Because it has no mapping from a workspace address to a kernel parameter, the
 loader rejects every nonzero workspace instead of allocating unused memory.
@@ -74,6 +83,10 @@ Argument validation and packing happen in `prepare_launch()` before graph
 capture. It returns a move-only `NvidiaLaunchPacket` owning stable, pre-sized
 eight-byte host slots, the parameter-pointer array and checked final grid.
 The packet itself is an execution lease and prevents unload.
+The slot is storage, not the declared device parameter width: dynamic sizes and
+strides remain four-byte `int32` kernel parameters inside zeroed eight-byte
+slots. Positive sizes and nonnegative strides are rejected before packet
+publication when they exceed `INT32_MAX`.
 
 Tensor operands provide a non-null opaque device address plus complete shape
 and element-stride metadata. Static dimensions/strides must match exactly;
